## 6\. Conclusion

In this tutorial, we’ve explored the architecture of MCP and Java SDK.  The main components are the _McpServer_, which exposes various functionalities that the _McpClient_ can use from within the _McpHost,_ while the transport channels and their details are handled by the _McpTransport._

Next, we explored primitives and the different types available on the server and the client.

Finally, we implemented one of the tools and verified the McpClient connection and invocation with both the MCP sample server and our local _McpServer_.

